-- title:
--   Residual Hecke eigensystem realised on a corner of H¹
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ (nonzero) and a set $S\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ containing no prime divisor of $N$, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring that is a characteristic-zero domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with residue field $k=$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪`; assume as a `Fact` that [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6) holds, i.e. the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule generated by those weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are integers is the whole space. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators attached to primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ and to primes $q\mid N$ with $q\notin S$, into $k$. On the $\mathcal{O}$-module [`CohCarrier.H1 N ⊤ 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162) consider the operators [`CohCarrier.opFamily N ⊤ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) indexed by [`CohCarrier.Gen N S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13), whose constructors are `T ℓ` for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$, `U q` for primes $q\mid N$, and `dia d` for $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/N)^{\times}$; assume these operators commute pairwise (`hcomm`). Let $\bar\theta:$ `Gen N S` $\to k$ satisfy $\bar\theta(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$, $\bar\theta(U_q)=\theta(U_q)$ (the hypothesis on $S$ supplying $q\notin S$) and $\bar\theta(\langle d\rangle)=1$. Let $B$ be the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}($`H1 N ⊤ 𝒪`$)$ generated by the range of `opFamily`, i.e. the `opSubalgebra` of the Hecke datum [`CohCarrier.hdata N ⊤ S 𝒪 k hcomm θbar`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L96), and let `Sp` be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of $B$: a family $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1}$ of complete orthogonal idempotents together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting all maximal ideals of $B$ and satisfying $e_i\in\mathfrak{m}_j\iff i\ne j$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0}Be_{i_0}$ to $k$ such that, for every generator $g$, $\pi_k(e_{i_0}\,\mathrm{op}(g)\,e_{i_0})=\bar\theta(g)$, where $\mathrm{op}(g)$ is the corresponding element of $B$.
--
--   This is the statement that a residual Hecke eigensystem of the weight-two cusp forms of level $N$ is realised, with the same eigenvalues, on a corner of the cohomological Hecke algebra acting on $H^1$ of the level group: a cohomological incarnation, in the style of Eichler–Shimura, of the passage from a character of the cusp-form Hecke algebra to a maximal ideal of the integral algebra of Hecke operators on cohomology. It is used in the construction of corner realisations of local Hecke algebras at squarefree level, via [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_isCornerRealization_and_linearEquiv_baseML_of_squarefree`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_isCornerRealization_and_linearEquiv_baseML_of_squarefree).
